-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 SCRIPT AND UTILITY:
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 - enKF.sh                     : Main script to orchestrate the assimilation run.
 - prepare_enssim_from_DA.sh   : Prepare an ensemble of str files without DA.
                                 It uses the DA files to retrieve info. Then
                                 use run_ens_shyfem_noDA.sh.
 - run_ens_shyfem_noDA.sh      : Runs multiple SHYFEM simulations using different 
                                 STR files (common basename) without DA.
 - process_ext.sh:               Splits DA or noDA .ext files, merges them by 
                                 variable, and generates ensemble statistics.
 - process_shy_analysis.sh     : Utility to merge all .shy files in analysis.
 - perturbe_state              : Generates an ensemble of perturbed RST files
 - perturbe_ts                 : Generates an ensemble of perturbed timeseries
                                 with one valyue and SHYFEM time notation
 - perturbe_fem_wind_press     : Generates an ensemble of perturbed FEM files
                                 from a wind&pressure FEM file
 - perturbe_fem_heat           : Generates an ensemble of perturbed FEM files
                                 from a heat FEM file
 - perturbe_fem_scalar         : Generates an ensemble of perturbed FEM files
                                 from a scalar (2D/3D) file (e.g., rain)
 - make_antime_list            : Creates the antime_list.txt for time series.
 - enKF2enKS                   : Kalman Smoother from Filter output. 
                                 NOTE: Incompatible with localization.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Before running the code
===================

Install all packages required to compile SHYFEM, compile the model, then
install the following software:
- parallel;
- liblapack-dev;
- libfftw3-dev.


Running the code
===================

To run the code, execute enKF.sh. The mandatory arguments are:

Usage: enKF.sh [method] [localisation] [n] [out]

- method = 11|12|13|21|22|23       (see analysis.f90)
- localisation = 0 (disable), 1 (enable)
- n = number of threads
- out = 0 saves only mean and std restarts
        1 saves all restarts (required by enKS)

Before running enKF.sh, prepare the following files:


----------
ens_list.txt
----------
List of SKEL files (used to create STR files) and initial restart files.

Example with one restart per member:

medit_73830_S6_000.skel restart_000.rst
medit_73830_S6_001.skel restart_001.rst
medit_73830_S6_002.skel restart_002.rst
...

Example using the same restart for the whole initial ensemble:

medit_73830_S6_000.skel restart_000.rst
medit_73830_S6_001.skel restart_000.rst
medit_73830_S6_002.skel restart_000.rst
...


----------
obs_list.txt
----------
Each line contains:
- a flag describing the observation type;
- the file name.
- x y z coordinates
- STD
- Rho (for local analysis and superobs)

Example:

0DLEV Ancona_obs_ass.dat 13.49 43.63 0. 0.1 1.
0DLEV Bari_obs_ass.dat 16.88 41.15 0. 0.1 1.
...

Supported flags:
- 0DLEV : sea level time series;
- 0DTEM : surface temperature time series;
- 0DSAL : surface salinity time series;
- 2DVEL : FEM-file with 2D surface currents (e.g., HF radar).


----------
antime_list.txt
----------
This file contains the analysis schedule.

First row: SHYFEM time and number of observation files
Second row: a 0-1 mask selecting observations used at that step
Following rows: same format for subsequent analysis times (in ascending order)

Use make_antime_list to generate this file automatically.
If unused, prescribe a mask of all 1 values for each time step.


----------
lbound.dat (optional)
----------
Recommended.
Controls how the analysis behaves near open boundaries:

- full background at boundary nodes;
- full analysis beyond a specified distance (G-C function).

Format:
first line : number of nodes
next lines : node_id   radius


----------
mod_err.info (optional - experimental)
----------
Enable by setting mode_an = 1 in mod_para.f90.

Defines red-noise model error parameters through an augmented state.

Warning: routine make_2Dpert currently gives a segmentation fault.

Format (one row):

  nx ny fmult theta rerror dt tau

Meaning:
- nx, ny   : grid size for pseudo-random fields
- fmult    : factor to create a supersample
- theta    : rotation angle (0 = East, anticlockwise)
- rerror   : relative model error (currently only water levels)
- dt       : time between observation steps
- tau      : e-folding time of the red noise


----------
skel files
----------
Skeleton files used to generate STR files during each analysis step.
They must match the restart file settings exactly.

Required content:

In section $title :
  the second line must contain the string: NAMESIM

In section $para :
  itanf  = 'ITANF'
  itend  = 'ITEND'
  itrst  = 'ITANF'
  idtrst = IDTRST     (no quotation marks)

In section $name :
  restrt = 'RESTRT'

To save results during the analysis, add in $para :
  itrst  = 'ITANF'
  itout  = 'ITANF'
  itext  = 'ITANF'
  itcon  = 'ITANF'
  itmflx = 'ITANF'

You can also use the SHYFEM utility rst2shy to generate SHY files from restarts.


----------
Initial restart files
----------
Each restart file must contain one record at the first analysis time.

The first restart is the control (unperturbed) run, i.e. ensemble member 0.

To create a good initial ensemble, run multiple simulations with perturbed
forcings and/or boundary conditions and save the restart at the first
analysis step.
The ensemble should be centered: mean approximately equal to control.


----------
Observation files
----------

1) Sea level time series:
string-time1 value1
string-time2 value2
...

2) Surface current fields (FEM-file):
Bad or missing values must be flagged with -999.


Parameters of the assimilation
===================

See the file mod_para.f90 for all assimilation parameters.
